Option 3: Weather Report  
Clouds are often associated with weather patterns and can be an important indicator of changing weather conditions. For example, if you see dark, thick clouds gathering on the horizon, it may be a sign of an approaching storm. These clouds can signal unsettled weather and the possibility of rain or thunderstorms. On the other hand, if you see light, fluffy clouds, it may be a sign of fair weather, suggesting that the day will remain calm and pleasant. Weather reports frequently mention clouds as they are a key component in forecasting weather changes.

