By implementing non-deterministic decision-making in this way, we can generate new patterns and trends in the data set. For example, if we analyze the user queries and responses over time, we can identify new patterns and trends that were not previously known, uncovering hidden structures or tendencies. This can lead to the discovery of new insights and improvements in the chatbot's performance, enhancing its ability to communicate effectively and adapt to user needs.

